Changed :meth:`Calendar.from_ical <icalendar.cal.calendar.Calendar.from_ical>` to raise :class:`~icalendar.error.ICalDecodeError` when the data is not valid UTF-8. Previously, it silently replaced the invalid bytes with ``�``. If you know the encoding of the data, decode it yourself before parsing, as described in :ref:`from-ical-not-utf-8`. I used AI to assist me with this change. @Hrittik20
